---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';

const portals = [
  { name: 'Patient', text: 'A view-only portal where patients follow their care plan, goals, and progress between visits.' },
  { name: 'Virtual Care Coordinator (VCC)', text: 'The daily workspace for care coordinators running monthly CCM outreach, documentation, and follow-up.' },
  { name: 'Doctor', text: 'Physician oversight of their patient panel, encounter review, and sign-off on monthly billing reports.' },
  { name: 'Admin', text: 'Organization-level management of users, roles, and operations across the platform.' },
];
---

<CaseStudy
  name="ClearPath Virtual Health"
  description="Case study: how Sām Kazemi architected ClearPath Virtual Health, a production HIPAA-compliant CCM/RPM platform with four role-based portals."
  summary="A production HIPAA-compliant chronic care management (CCM) and remote patient monitoring (RPM) platform that helps patients stay on track and helps providers deliver better care between visits."
  role="Lead Software Engineer: architecture, frontend, cloud, team lead"
  org="MedManage Solutions"
  period="Sep 2025 – Present"
  status="Live in production"
  live="https://clearpathvirtualhealth.com/"
  liveLabel="clearpathvirtualhealth.com"
  stack={[
    'React',
    'JavaScript',
    'React Router',
    'Tailwind CSS',
    'Material UI',
    'REST APIs (JWT)',
    'RBAC',
    'MFA',
    'AWS S3',
    'AWS CloudFront',
    'AWS ECS Fargate',
    'CI/CD',
    'PDF export',
    'HIPAA',
    'CPT / ICD-10',
  ]}
>
  <section class="reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">The challenge</p>
    <h2>Chronic care happens between visits</h2>
    <p>
      Patients living with chronic conditions need support every month, not only when they are in
      the exam room. Medicare’s Chronic Care Management program pays for that ongoing coordination,
      but only when the work is documented precisely, time is tracked accurately, and a physician
      signs off.
    </p>
    <p>
      The platform had to serve four very different users with strict boundaries between what each
      of them can see and do, hold up to HIPAA, and produce billing records that stand up to
      Medicare, all without adding work to clinicians’ days.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">My role</p>
    <h2>Architected from the ground up</h2>
    <p>
      I architected and built ClearPath from the ground up and lead its ongoing development: designing
      scalable features, improving clinical workflows with the care team, and managing a distributed
      engineering team. I own the frontend across all four portals and its integration with the
      platform’s secure APIs, and I work across the AWS infrastructure and delivery pipeline.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">What I built</p>
    <h2>Four portals, one platform</h2>
    <p>
      ClearPath spans 30+ components across four role-based portals, each scoped to exactly what that
      role needs.
    </p>
    <ul class="cs-flow">
      {
        portals.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <div>
              <strong>{p.name}</strong>
              <span>{p.text}</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <div class="cs-features">
      <div class="card">
        <span class="icon-badge"><Icon name="lock" /></span>
        <h3>Security and compliance</h3>
        <p>
          HIPAA-compliant session management, multi-factor authentication, and audit logging, with
          JWT-authenticated REST APIs and role-based access control at every boundary.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="icon-badge"><Icon name="file-text" /></span>
        <h3>Monthly CCM billing reports</h3>
        <p>
          Encounter documentation, CPT and ICD-10 code management, physician sign-off workflows, and
          PDF export, directly supporting Medicare reimbursement compliance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="icon-badge"><Icon name="users" /></span>
        <h3>Patient engagement and care coordination</h3>
        <p>
          End-to-end workflows that keep patients connected to their care team between visits, from
          outreach and scheduling to follow-up.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="icon-badge"><Icon name="cloud" /></span>
        <h3>Cloud and delivery</h3>
        <p>
          AWS infrastructure on S3, CloudFront, and ECS Fargate, shipped through automated CI/CD
          pipelines.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Impact</p>
    <h2>Measurable results for the business and for patients</h2>
    <ul class="cs-metrics">
      <li><strong>200%+</strong><span>increase in recurring revenue</span></li>
      <li><strong>15%</strong><span>fewer missed appointments</span></li>
      <li><strong>40%</strong><span>less administrative overhead</span></li>
      <li><strong>35%</strong><span>faster deployments</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">What I learned</p>
    <h2>In healthcare, correctness is the feature</h2>
    <p>
      A billing code, a timestamp, or a permission check that is slightly wrong is not a cosmetic
      bug. It affects patient care and Medicare compliance. Building ClearPath taught me to design for
      that: strict role boundaries, defensive handling of every piece of data, and a delivery process
      where nothing ships without passing its checks.
    </p>
  </section>
</CaseStudy>
